e49f29c8c75ee65657db12f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.960b0b92aef0a7c98e49f29c8c75ee65657db12f.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Warning","headline":"Flash Flood Warning issued October 22 at 12:31PM MDT until October 22 at 3:30PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"FFWGJT\n\nThe National Weather Service in Grand Junction has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nNortheastern San Miguel County in southwestern Colorado...\nSoutheastern Montrose County in west central Colorado...\n\n* Until 330 PM MDT.\n\n* At 1231 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nthunderstorms producing heavy rain across the warned area. Heavy\nrainfall rates are occurring on already saturated ground as this\narea has received between 1 and 2 inches of rain over the last 24\nhours. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Radar and automated gauges.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams,\nurban areas, highways, streets and underpasses.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nNorwood, Sawpit, Placerville and Fall Creek.","ends":"2026-10-22T15:30:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Montrose, CO; San Miguel, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e7e2d7b92b82ed6e9a37e823a77ed17822e660ac.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e7e2d7b92b82ed6e9a37e823a77ed17822e660ac.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-22T19:15:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 221915 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 115 PM MDT Thu Oct 22 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Widespread rain continues through early Friday. - Flooding/Flash Flooding is likely across portions of southwest Colorado and southeast Utah. - Modeled responses suggest several rivers reaching bankfull or higher at river forecast points across southwest C","